    "last_model_intent_unverified": "The fix is complete and verified.\n\n**Diagnosis:** `requests.exceptions.JSONDecodeError` inherits from both `InvalidJSONError` (a `RequestException`) and `json.JSONDecodeError`. The base `RequestException.__reduce__` (from `IOError`/`Exception`) reconstructs the exception by calling `self.__class__(*self.args)`. But `JSONDecodeError.__init__` expects the JSON-specific signature `(msg, doc, pos)`, while `self.args` holds the `RequestException`-style args — so unpickling raised a `TypeError` about missing constructor arguments.\n\n**Repair:** Added a `__reduce__` to `JSONDecodeError` that reconstructs via `self.__class__(self.msg, self.doc, self.pos)`, preserving the exception type, message, original document, and error position across a pickle round trip.\n\n**V…",
